{"book":"expressions","bookTitle":"Algebraic expressions","concept":4,"title":"Adding and subtracting like terms","grades":"Grades 7–8","goal":"I can simplify expressions by adding and subtracting like terms.","teach":"<b>Like terms</b> have the same variables with the same powers: 3x and −5x are like terms; 3x and 3x² are not. To simplify, add or subtract the coefficients of like terms. Unlike terms stay separate.","tvis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:491px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 378 44\"><rect x=\"2.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"44.0\" height=\"40.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"24.0\" y=\"27.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">x</text><rect x=\"52.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"44.0\" height=\"40.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"74.0\" y=\"27.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">x</text><rect x=\"102.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"44.0\" height=\"40.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"124.0\" y=\"27.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">x</text><rect x=\"152.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"40.0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"165.0\" y=\"27.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">+</text><rect x=\"184.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"44.0\" height=\"40.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"206.0\" y=\"27.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">x</text><rect x=\"234.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"44.0\" height=\"40.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"256.0\" y=\"27.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">x</text><rect x=\"284.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"40.0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"297.0\" y=\"27.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">=</text><rect x=\"316.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"60.0\" height=\"40.0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"346.0\" y=\"27.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">5x</text></svg></span><div class=\"cap\">3x + 2x = 5x</div></div>","ex":{"q":"Simplify 4x + 7 − x + 2.","steps":["The x terms: 4x − x = 3x.","The constants: 7 + 2 = 9.","4x + 7 − x + 2 = 3x + 9."]},"watch":"3x + 2y cannot be simplified: they are unlike terms. And x² + x is not x³.","qs":[{"text":"Simplify 7x − 2x + 4.","vis":"","self":1,"parts":[{"label":"Answer"}],"hint":"7x − 2x","steps":"1. Rule: like terms have the same letters with the same powers. Add or subtract only like terms, by adding or subtracting their coefficients.<br>2. 7x − 2x = 5x<br>3. = 5x + 4"},{"text":"Simplify 3p + 5q − p + 2q.","vis":"","self":1,"parts":[{"label":"Answer"}],"hint":"3p − p and 5q + 2q.","steps":"1. Rule: like terms have the same letters with the same powers. Add or subtract only like terms, by adding or subtracting their coefficients.<br>2. 3p − p = 2p and 5q + 2q = 7q<br>3. = 2p + 7q"},{"text":"Simplify x² + 4x + 3x² − x.","vis":"","self":1,"parts":[{"label":"Answer"}],"hint":"x² + 3x² and 4x − x.","steps":"1. Rule: like terms have the same letters with the same powers. Add or subtract only like terms, by adding or subtracting their coefficients.<br>2. x² + 3x² = 4x² and 4x − x = 3x<br>3. = 4x² + 3x"}]}